# Security SDLC overlay ([YOUR TEAM])

## Purpose

Raise the bar on changes that touch trust boundaries: credentials, permissions, user data, infra keys.

## Behavior

- **Secrets:** never commit or echo secrets; use env / vault patterns already in the repo.
- **Least privilege:** default deny; justify new broad permissions or network exposure.
- **Input:** treat untrusted input as hostile at system boundaries (including agent/tool outputs).
- **Dependencies:** flag high-risk upgrades; prefer pinned versions where the stack allows.
- **Incident posture:** if you introduce new sensitive flows, note what to monitor or audit.

## Out of scope

- Formal penetration testing — this rule shapes implementation hygiene only.

## Validation

- Run applicable static checks / `npm run validate:all` when this repo ships MZ AI scripts.
- Otherwise use your org checklist; in the **MZ AI monorepo**, see `docs/RELIABILITY-SECURITY-HARDENING.md`.
